[b]QLC+ Swiss Knife v1.4.0 — build your next show with the tool[/b]

Hi all, a new release of Swiss Knife, the free companion toolkit for QLC+ 5 workspaces (not affiliated with the QLC+ project).

With v1.4.0 [b]Quick Start, Function Porter and Show Book leave Alpha[/b]. Everything they write is checked before it is saved, tested against real show files, and your original files are never changed.

[b]What's new[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Workspace Doctor[/b] — a health check for any .qxw: duplicate IDs, broken references, looks leaking into each other (LTP), strobe/auto-programs left on, missing PANIC RESET, MIDI buttons without a controller patched, unused functions.
[*][b]Start a new rig from an existing show[/b] — build the rig in Quick Start, then "Port from an existing show": looks, effects and their buttons come across, even to [b]other fixture types[/b] (dimmer, RGB ↔ colour wheel, pan/tilt angles, strobe, gobo are translated).
[*][b]Function Porter brings the Virtual Console[/b] — pages, frames and buttons, placed without overlapping; fan-in for smaller rigs (14 → 6 fixtures); stage plans of both rigs; a port report next to the new file.
[*][b]MIDI / key control comes along[/b] — bindings, the controller's input patch and profile; move bindings to another universe.
[*][b]Show Book[/b] — PDF/CSV show paperwork with the Virtual Console page by page (frames, positions, key/MIDI bindings) and a Doctor summary.
[*]Quick Start: mode-aware scenes with safe neutral values, a PANIC RESET that really resets, fixture groups with their own dimmer, looks and effects.
[/list]

Download and release notes: [url=https://github.com/giopas/qlc-plus-swiss-knife-tool-script/releases/tag/v1.4.0]GitHub release v1.4.0[/url]
Documentation: [url=https://github.com/giopas/qlc-plus-swiss-knife-tool-script/wiki]Wiki[/url]

Tested with QLC+ 5.2.2 (and 4.14 for Quick Start output). Feedback and bug reports are very welcome on the [url=https://github.com/giopas/qlc-plus-swiss-knife-tool-script/issues]issues page[/url].
